    <string name="item_flavor_1">The first courier off the line. Light, patient, and never late.</string>
    <string name="item_flavor_2">Carries the small envelopes nobody else will fly after dark.</string>
    <string name="item_flavor_3">Awarded for crates hauled through a climbing sky.</string>
    <string name="item_flavor_4">Built to ride the edge of a storm lane and keep the cargo dry.</string>
    <string name="item_flavor_5">Given to pilots who know exactly when to burn the tank.</string>
    <string name="item_flavor_6">Gold trim, warm engine glow, and a habit of landing rich.</string>
    <string name="item_flavor_7">Struck for a run flown under the northern lights.</string>
    <string name="item_flavor_8">Thin air, long glide, and a view of the curve of the world.</string>
    <string name="item_flavor_9">First light on the fuselage after a night of secured runs.</string>
    <string name="item_flavor_10">Worn by pilots who flew straight through the gate and lived.</string>
    <string name="item_flavor_11">Silver for the long reach, awarded once the crates stop counting.</string>
    <string name="item_flavor_12">The mark of a pilot the tower stops questioning.</string>

